# STATUS: LIVE, 2026-11-17. Inputs of the open FFmpeg/DCGM rows (docs/design/V3_OPEN_ROWS_FFMPEG_DCGM.md section 3 names the trust anchor of each).
# Data only, sourced by provision.sh. Owner rule 2026-11-17: no sha256 of a downloaded binary is pinned in git. What is pinned here is a
# source commit (anchor: the upstream git history), an exact package VERSION string (not a hash), and URLs of the upstream's own origin.
#
# nvcodec_probe.c headers: nv-codec-headers (MIT), a source input pinned by upstream tag AND full commit (pin_lib.sh checks HEAD == commit).
OPENROWS_NVCH_URL=https://github.com/FFmpeg/nv-codec-headers.git
OPENROWS_NVCH_TAG=n12.2.72.0
OPENROWS_NVCH_COMMIT=c69278340ab1d5559c7d7bf0edf615dc33ddbba7
# DCGM: NVIDIA's own apt repository. The repository key is fetched at run time from NVIDIA's official URL (the same origin as the packages,
# over https) and installed as the repository's signed-by key; apt then verifies the signed index. Pinned: the exact version string, which
# apt resolves (every DCGM 4 package depends on the same `= version` of its siblings). CUDA 12 flavour: it runs on any driver that
# supports CUDA 12 or newer.
OPENROWS_NVIDIA_REPO_BASE=https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/repos
OPENROWS_NVIDIA_KEY_FILE=3bf863cc.pub
OPENROWS_DCGM_VERSION=1:4.8.0-1
OPENROWS_DCGM_PACKAGE_STEMS="datacenter-gpu-manager-4-cuda datacenter-gpu-manager-4-proprietary-cuda"
